<p><a href="http://civgene.matthewnewhall.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/01/wheat.jpg"><img class="size-medium wp-image-1396 aligncenter" alt="wheat" src="http://civgene.matthewnewhall.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/01/wheat-300x168.jpg" width="300" height="168" /></a></p>
<p>&#8220;Likewise, adults that were prenatally exposed to famine conditions have also been reported to have significantly higher incidence of schizophrenia.&#8221;</p>
<p>Looks like support for another civgene theory. <a title="Is conspiracy theory useful?" href="http://civgene.matthewnewhall.com/archives/1297">That schizophrenia is genetic resistance to manipulation by psychopaths.</a> In this case epigeneticly triggered by starvation of an unborn&#8217;s mother.  Starvation, has a strong likelyhood it&#8217;s been caused by a collapsing economy.  Civgene predicts <a href="http://civgene.matthewnewhall.com/papers/Psychopaths-ancient-breed.html">economic collapses are because the percentage of psychopaths in the economy has grown too large.</a></p>
